  "facts": [
    "Charles Grimes Bridge opened as the Johnson Street Bridge on 4 August 1978, costing roughly $30 million and initially named after the construction project before being renamed in 1983.",
    "The bridge’s five 33.5‑metre main spans required computer analysis to manage their complex geometry, a pioneering use of technology in Australian bridge design at the time.",
    "In 1999‑2001, the north end was rebuilt on an easterly curve to link to the newly upgraded Flinders Street, reflecting the Docklands redevelopment’s shift from Footscray Road to Harbour Esplanade."
